The French Supermarket 
Supply Chain Hack (October 2026)

Over 300 French supermarkets 
(including chains like E. Leclerc, Intermarché, and Carrefour) using 
connected temperature management software

Hackers breached the remote refrigeration software 
and sent commands to forcefully heat up commercial fridges 
and freezers up to 50°C (120°F) overnight

Millions of euros worth of fresh and frozen food spoiled 
instantly across hundreds of locations
